<https://github.com/bioconda/bioconda-recipes/tree/master/recipes/reparation_blast> a ns1:SoftwareApplication ;
    ns1:alternateName "A pipeline that detects novel open reading frames with ribseq data for bacteria." ;
    ns1:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalTool/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    ns1:description "A pipeline that uses ribosome profiling data for a de novo open reading frame delineation in prokaryotic (bacterial) genomes. I changed the original reparation project to use the open-source blast tool (https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi) instead of the commercial usearch --ublast tool (https://drive5.com/usearch/manual/ublast_algo.html). I did this in order to add this tool to bioconda without having licensing issues with the commercial usearch -ublast tool. The original software was created at VIB-UGent Center for Medical Biotechnology and Lab of Bioinformatics and Computational Genomics (Biobix), University of Gent, Belgium, by Elvis Ndah. (https://github.com/Biobix/REPARATION). Be advised that the adapted version has slightly different results and is slower than the original reparation software." ;
    ns1:downloadUrl <https://github.com/RickGelhausen/REPARATION_blast/archive/v1.0.9.tar.gz> ;
    ns1:identifier <https://github.com/bioconda/bioconda-recipes/tree/master/recipes/reparation_blast> ;
    ns1:license "GPL3" ;
    ns1:name "reparation_blast" ;
    ns1:provider <https://bioconda.github.io/> ;
    ns1:softwareRequirements <https://github.com/bioconda/bioconda-recipes/tree/master/recipes/biopython>,
        <https://github.com/bioconda/bioconda-recipes/tree/master/recipes/blast>,
        <https://github.com/bioconda/bioconda-recipes/tree/master/recipes/glimmer>,
        <https://github.com/bioconda/bioconda-recipes/tree/master/recipes/openssl>,
        <https://github.com/bioconda/bioconda-recipes/tree/master/recipes/perl>,
        <https://github.com/bioconda/bioconda-recipes/tree/master/recipes/perl-bioperl>,
        <https://github.com/bioconda/bioconda-recipes/tree/master/recipes/perl-posix>,
        <https://github.com/bioconda/bioconda-recipes/tree/master/recipes/plastid>,
        <https://github.com/bioconda/bioconda-recipes/tree/master/recipes/prodigal>,
        <https://github.com/bioconda/bioconda-recipes/tree/master/recipes/pysam>,
